{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.MassTheory.AggregatorConvexityDichotomy","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.MassTheory.AggregatorConvexityDichotomy","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.Convex.Function"],"declarations":10,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.AggregatorConvexity.wMult_b3_eq_zero_iff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.AggregatorConvexity.wMult_b3_eq_zero_iff","kind":"theorem","line":181,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/AggregatorConvexityDichotomy.lean#L181-L197","doc":"**And it vanishes only when the bonds do not couple.** On `f > −2` the\nmultiplicative cumulant is zero exactly at `f = 1`, i.e. exactly when every bond\nfactor is trivial. So within this assembly there is no tuning of `f` that\nrecovers a positive `b₃` — the boundary is the decoupled system. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.AggregatorConvexity.wMult_b3_nonpos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.AggregatorConvexity.wMult_b3_nonpos","kind":"theorem","line":172,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/AggregatorConvexityDichotomy.lean#L172-L179","doc":"**Unconditional non-positivity in the equal-bond case.** No threshold on `f`\nis needed beyond `f > −2`, which every genuine bond factor satisfies. This is\nstrictly sharper than `MayerThreeBodySign.b3_neg_of_le`, which concluded from the\nmeasured `f_pn ≤ 2/3`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.AggregatorConvexity.wMult_b3_factor","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.AggregatorConvexity.wMult_b3_factor","kind":"theorem","line":164,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/AggregatorConvexityDichotomy.lean#L164-L170","doc":"**The multiplicative 3-body cumulant factors as a negated perfect square.**\n`(1 − f³) − 3(1 − f) = −(f − 1)²(f + 2)`. The sign is therefore *second order*\nin the coupling `1 − f`, not a consequence of where the measured bond factor\nsits. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.AggregatorConvexity.wMult","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.AggregatorConvexity.wMult","kind":"def","line":160,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/AggregatorConvexityDichotomy.lean#L160-L162","doc":"The multiplicative (Mayer) weight of an `n`-bond system at common bond\nfactor `f`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.AggregatorConvexity.b3Agg_sq_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.AggregatorConvexity.b3Agg_sq_pos","kind":"theorem","line":149,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/AggregatorConvexityDichotomy.lean#L149-L153","doc":"**Non-vacuity of the convex branch.** A strictly convex aggregator does reach\na positive cumulant, so `not_concaveOn_of_b3Agg_pos` is not excluding the target\nalong with the class. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.AggregatorConvexity.b3Agg_linear_eq_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.AggregatorConvexity.b3Agg_linear_eq_zero","kind":"theorem","line":142,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/AggregatorConvexityDichotomy.lean#L142-L147","doc":"**The additive assembly is the boundary case.** An affine-through-the-origin\naggregator — the bond-functional sum — saturates both bounds at `b₃ = 0`. This\nreaches the value of `QOU.Mass.PairwiseCumulantVanishing.b3_eq_zero_ofBondFunctional`\nby a different route; it is a numerical agreement, not a reduction of it. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.AggregatorConvexity.not_concaveOn_of_b3Agg_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.AggregatorConvexity.not_concaveOn_of_b3Agg_pos","kind":"theorem","line":134,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/AggregatorConvexityDichotomy.lean#L134-L140","doc":"**The exclusion, as the programme uses it.** A strictly positive 3-body\ncumulant — which is what AME2020 measures, `b₃ = +1.4262225` — refutes concavity\nof the aggregator on `[0, ∞)`, whatever the bond weight and bond set. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.AggregatorConvexity.b3Agg_nonneg_of_convexOn","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.AggregatorConvexity.b3Agg_nonneg_of_convexOn","kind":"theorem","line":119,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/AggregatorConvexityDichotomy.lean#L119-L132","doc":"**A convex aggregator through the origin cannot produce a negative one.**\nThe dual of `b3Agg_nonpos_of_concaveOn`, and the half that says the target sign\nis reachable at all. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.AggregatorConvexity.b3Agg_nonpos_of_concaveOn","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.AggregatorConvexity.b3Agg_nonpos_of_concaveOn","kind":"theorem","line":103,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/AggregatorConvexityDichotomy.lean#L103-L117","doc":"**A concave aggregator through the origin cannot produce a positive 3-body\ncumulant.** Jensen at `0` and `3g` with weights `(2/3, 1/3)`. No hypothesis on\nthe bond set enters: `g` is the common bond weight and `3` the three-body bond\ncount, and the argument is one secant comparison. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.AggregatorConvexity.b3Agg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.AggregatorConvexity.b3Agg","kind":"def","line":95,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/AggregatorConvexityDichotomy.lean#L95-L101","doc":"The connected 3-body Ursell cumulant of a symmetric binding assembled as\n`B(A) = Φ(m_A · g)` with bond counts `m_2 = 1`, `m_3 = 3` and `Φ 0 = 0`:\n\n    b₃ = B(3) − 3·B(2) = Φ(3g) − 3·Φ(g).\n\nA secant comparison on the ray through the origin. ","signatureChunk":0}]}